    "maxProducts": 1000,
    "_maxProductsNote": "RAISED 700 -> 1000 on 2026-09-12: measured 656 stored = 94% of the 700 cap, and truncation EXCLUDES ASINs silently (logged at warn, nothing fails) — the same class of defect as the priority lane's slice(0,20). Cost of the headroom is NOT a longer ASIN-sweep lap (an earlier note here claimed that and was wrong: _runAsinSweep walks _knownProducts, which maxProducts does not bound — truncation happens in base.js run(), AFTER fetchProducts, so the lap was always over the full catalogue). The real cost is the per-poll Redis pipeline, up to 1000 SETs every 6s. IMPORTANT for any future raise: raising a cap that is ACTIVELY truncating releases the truncated tail, which stale cleanup has already written inStock:false — that would fire a wave of false RESTOCKs. Safe at 700->1000 only because the measured 656 was under 700, so nothing was being truncated. Original note: catalogue is ~613 and grows ~130/day; the default 500 cap silently deleted the alphabetical tail (113 rows) every poll, which is why the 30th Celebration ASINs (B0H7*) never alerted — they sort at 584-589. Raise this BEFORE the catalogue reaches it: truncation is logged at warn but nothing fails.",
